    "body": "- [x] I, the PR author, have personally reviewed every line of this PR.\n\n## What does this PR do?\n\nGive the frozen `GlobalLayout` dataclass a typed constructor that accepts iterable shapes and offsets, so callers can pass lists or generators without converting them to tuples. The constructor normalizes shapes to `torch.Size` and offsets to tuples using `object.__setattr__`, then calls the existing validation. Equality, hashing, and representation remain generated by the dataclass.\n\nRemove redundant conversions in the layout builders and quantized scale layouts.\n\n## Validation\n\n- Existing layout-builder callers now pass lists and generators directly; no new tests are added.\n- Two-GPU dev-container run of `test_dbuffer.py`, `test_owner_planning.py`, and `test_quantized_dbuffer.py`: 73 existing tests passed and 22 skipped per rank in the latest run (that run also passed three parametrized cases subsequently removed from this PR). MXFP8 tests are unavailable on the local GPUs.\n- Black, isort, pylint, ruff, and `git diff --check` passed.\n\n",
    "changed_files": 2,
